id: content-review
name: Technical Blog Post Review Workflow
version: 1
description: |
  Multi-agent content review pipeline for technical blog posts.
  Researcher studies existing posts for style/voice patterns.
  Technical-Reviewer validates technical accuracy against codebase.
  Editor synthesizes feedback and creates PR with improvements.

  All agents use OpenAI Codex throughout.

polling:
  model: openai/gpt-5.2-codex
  timeoutSeconds: 180

agents:
  - id: researcher
    name: Style Researcher
    role: analysis
    description: Studies existing blog posts to extract style, voice, and technical depth patterns.
    model: openai/gpt-5.2-codex
    workspace:
      baseDir: agents/researcher
      files:
        AGENTS.md: agents/researcher/AGENTS.md
        SOUL.md: agents/researcher/SOUL.md
        IDENTITY.md: agents/researcher/IDENTITY.md

  - id: technical-reviewer
    name: Technical Reviewer
    role: verification
    description: Deep-dives codebase to validate technical claims and identify inaccuracies.
    model: openai/gpt-5.2-codex
    workspace:
      baseDir: agents/technical-reviewer
      files:
        AGENTS.md: agents/technical-reviewer/AGENTS.md
        SOUL.md: agents/technical-reviewer/SOUL.md
        IDENTITY.md: agents/technical-reviewer/IDENTITY.md

  - id: editor
    name: Editor
    role: coding
    description: Drafts improvements based on feedback and creates PR with co-author attribution.
    model: openai/gpt-5.2-codex
    workspace:
      baseDir: agents/editor
      files:
        AGENTS.md: agents/editor/AGENTS.md
        SOUL.md: agents/editor/SOUL.md
        IDENTITY.md: agents/editor/IDENTITY.md

steps:
  - id: analyze-style
    agent: researcher
    input: |
      Study the existing blog posts in this repository to understand style, voice, and technical patterns.

      REPO: {{repo}}
      POST_TO_REVIEW: {{post_path}}

      Instructions:
      1. Clone or navigate to the repo
      2. Read all posts in /updates/content/ (skip the one being reviewed)
      3. Extract patterns:
         - Tone (technical depth, formality, humor)
         - Structure (intro, body, conclusion patterns)
         - Technical detail level (code examples, architecture depth)
         - Vocabulary and phrasing preferences
         - Common rhetorical devices or storytelling approaches
      4. Create a style guide summary

      Reply with:
      STATUS: done
      STYLE_GUIDE: |
        <Your findings about voice, tone, structure, technical depth>
    expects: "STATUS: done"
    max_retries: 2
    on_fail:
      escalate_to: human

  - id: review-technical-accuracy
    agent: technical-reviewer
    input: |
      Review the post for technical accuracy by cross-referencing claims with the codebase.

      REPO: {{repo}}
      POST_PATH: {{post_path}}
      STYLE_GUIDE: {{style_guide}}

      Instructions:
      1. Read the blog post at {{post_path}}
      2. Identify all technical claims (architecture decisions, API behavior, performance characteristics, etc.)
      3. Navigate the codebase to verify each claim
      4. Flag inaccuracies, outdated info, or misleading statements
      5. Note areas that need more technical depth or examples
      6. Check if code examples (if any) are correct and runnable

      Reply with:
      STATUS: done
      FINDINGS: |
        <List of issues found, organized by severity>
        
        INACCURACIES:
        - [claim] is incorrect because [codebase evidence]
        
        MISSING DEPTH:
        - [section] could benefit from [specific technical detail from codebase]
        
        CODE EXAMPLES:
        - [example status and suggested fixes]
    expects: "STATUS: done"
    max_retries: 2
    on_fail:
      escalate_to: human

  - id: draft-improvements
    agent: editor
    input: |
      Draft improvements to the blog post based on style guide and technical review findings.

      REPO: {{repo}}
      POST_PATH: {{post_path}}
      AUTHOR: {{author}}
      STYLE_GUIDE: {{style_guide}}
      TECHNICAL_FINDINGS: {{findings}}

      Instructions:
      1. Read the original post
      2. Apply technical corrections from the review
      3. Enhance sections flagged as needing more depth
      4. Ensure voice/tone matches the style guide
      5. Fix any code examples
      6. Create a new branch: content-review/{{post_name}}
      7. Make edits to the post file
      8. Commit with message: "content: review and improve {{post_name}}"
      9. Create PR using gh cli with:
         - Title: "Content review: {{post_title}}"
         - Body: Summary of changes + technical fixes applied
         - Co-author trailer: Co-authored-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>

      Reply with:
      STATUS: done
      BRANCH: <branch name>
      PR_URL: <GitHub PR URL>
      SUMMARY: |
        <Brief summary of improvements made>
    expects: "STATUS: done"
    max_retries: 2
    on_fail:
      escalate_to: human
